{{!--
    The "N of M MCP tools available" line, shown by every page that mints an MCP token so the
    three cannot disagree about what a credential will actually be offered. The counting rule is
    uiMcpToolCount() in static/js/ui.js - the browser's copy of toolVisibleTo(), pinned to it by
    test/mcp-tools-test.js. Reads mcpTools (and mcpSections, when auto-wired) from the page
    context.

    Pass manageName (and the mail controls) to have ui.js drive the count from the section
    radios (the MCP config generator and the consent prompt); leave them out and the page
    repaints the element itself, which is what the access-token form does.
    Params:
      id         - element id (required; the page's own script needs it, and so does nothing else)
      manageName - the management level radio group name, for the auto-wired pages (optional)
      mailName   - the mail level radio group name (optional, with manageName)
      mailToggle - id of the checkbox that switches the mail section on (optional, with mailName)
      accountId  - id of the "limit to one account" field to follow (optional, with manageName)
      class      - extra classes on the wrapper (optional)
--}}
<div id="{{id}}" class="text-sm space-y-1{{#if class}} {{class}}{{/if}}" data-mcp-tools="{{json mcpTools}}"
    {{#if manageName}}data-mcp-manage-name="{{manageName}}" data-mcp-mail-name="{{mailName}}"
    data-mcp-mail-toggle="{{mailToggle}}" data-mcp-account-id="{{accountId}}"
    data-mcp-sections="{{json mcpSections}}"{{/if}}></div>
